  "English edition · Prepared 14 October 2026": "",
  "Before you enter": "",
  "A map is a way to connect ideas.": "",
  "The goal is to explain what changes, who is affected, and which conditions transmit the change. Like revealing terrain in an exploration game, each region gives the next one context. Real economies also contain uncertainty, competing objectives, and rules that evolve.": "",
  "Economics": "",
  "How people organize scarce resources, produce goods and services, and distribute income.": "",
  "Finance": "",
  "How payments, funding, ownership claims, and risk connect decisions across time.": "",
  "Modules 3–7 form the main learning plan. Foundations 1–2 supply the supporting concepts. Numerical examples are hypothetical; policy institutions and legal protections differ across countries. The guide teaches mechanisms rather than prescribing trades or predicting prices.": "",
